  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry weather prevails for the rest of this week\nwith moderating temperatures. Next rain chance late in the \nweekend into early next week.\n\n\nHigh pressure that was settled just north of the region this\nmorning will continue to slide to the northeast throughout the\nevening and into Wednesday morning. This will allow for another\nnight of clear skies and predominantly calm winds across the\nregion. Under these conditions, radiational cooling will again\nbe efficient enough for temperatures to drop into the low to mid\n40s areawide, with upper 30s possible in isolated mountain\nlocations such as Burkes Garden. \n\nAs the aforementioned high pressure lifts to the northeast,\nwinds will eventually transition to out of the south/southwest.\nIn conjunction with this, 500mb heights will rise slightly\nacross the area as upper level ridging builds slightly over the\nSoutheast. This will allow for a gradual warmth in temperatures\nthrough the middle of the work week, with highs climbing back\ninto the low to mid 70s across Mountain locations, and low to\nmid 80s across Piedmont locations. \n\nBy Thursday night, a dry cold front looks to push through the\nregion as an upper level trough slides east through the Great\nLakes region on Thursday. This will moderate temperatures back\ninto the low 70s for Mountain locations and mid to upper 70s for\nPiedmont locations. Overall, dry and predominantly cloud free \nto partly cloudy weather looks to continue across the region \nthrough the end of the work week. \n\nBy Saturday, the forecast looks to become slightly more\nuncertain as it depends heavily on the track and timing of the\nlow pressure system in the Bay of Campeche in the Gulf. Most\nGEFS and ECMWF ensembles have rain chances increasing late \nSaturday into early Sunday morning from this system. The overall\ntrack of this system will greatly influence the amount of \nrainfall expected across the region, with the GEFS mean \nprecipitation values currently forecast at around 1.0\"-1.5\" \nareawide at this time. \n\nOverall, with this system still not developed yet, but currently\nforming, this portion of the forecast for the late weekend \nstill remains uncertain and low confidence at this time.",
